(1461712, 190001, 35548, '<td valign="top">Boy, I''m sure you are going to hear it about this image being to small, but not from me.  I have spend a life time printing small images in the darkroom and love small personal photograph.  I know how hard it is to take a photo like this especially with a digital camera that most likely has some shutter lag time....I hope my 10 boosts your score, this is a beautiful image. Thanks for showing it to us.</td>', 'Boy, I''m sure you are going to hear it about this image being to small, but not from me.  I have spend a life time printing small images in the darkroom and love small personal photograph.  I know how hard it is to take a photo like this especially with a digital camera that most likely has some shutter lag time....I hope my 10 boosts your score, this is a beautiful image. Thanks for showing it to us.', '2005-06-16 20:36:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1461713, 190125, 20530, '<td valign="top">Like the shallow DOF, though it might be a little too shallow? Like it.</td>', 'Like the shallow DOF, though it might be a little too shallow? Like it.', '2005-06-16 20:37:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(1461714, 190293, 11923, '<td valign="top">Great idea!  I think this meets the challenge very well, after all what''s more dark than not being able to see at all?   I think greater focus so the image was much sharper would help this quite a bit.  Also, perhaps adding in fingers "reading" the braille might give the image another point of interest for the viewer as well as make it that much more personal as it seems to be missing.. something - at least for me.  On a personal level for myself, I think it would do well in a black &amp; white image to give it a feeling of loss of sight/color as well, just another layer of darkness so to speak.  All in all I gave a 4.</td>', 'Great idea!  I think this meets the challenge very well, after all what''s more dark than not being able to see at all?   I think greater focus so the image was much sharper would help this quite a bit.  Also, perhaps adding in fingers "reading" the braille might give the image another point of interest for the viewer as well as make it that much more personal as it seems to be missing.. something - at least for me.  On a personal level for myself, I think it would do well in a black & white image to give it a feeling of loss of sight/color as well, just another layer of darkness so to speak.  All in all I gave a 4.', '2005-06-16 20:37:26.000000', NULL, 1),
