(1470879, 188078, 5792, '<td valign="top">Unique coloring, action pose and good use of the rule of thirds. Different interpretation of the challenge topic. Overall photographic quality is good.<br/> <br/>Your presentation very interesting. The use of blur to convey the sense of action by your model is a very interesting idea that wil work for some viewers but not for others.</td>', 'Unique coloring, action pose and good use of the rule of thirds. Different interpretation of the challenge topic. Overall photographic quality is good. Your presentation very interesting. The use of blur to convey the sense of action by your model is a very interesting idea that wil work for some viewers but not for others.', '2005-06-21 09:54:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470880, 190231, 36487, '<td valign="top">wow</td>', 'wow', '2005-06-21 09:59:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470885, 190010, 5792, '<td valign="top">Outstanding clarity. Good tonal range. B&amp;W is a good choice of presentation. You are to be commended for including very, very faint detail. Interesting way to convey the idea of darkness.<br/> <br/>The outstanding photographic quality is the strength of your image. Most viewers will understand it fits the challenge, but there will be a few that do not.<br/> <br/>The rightmost candle is a little overexposed which will hold down your score slightly.<br/> <br/>Overall this is an outstanding image that should score decently if studied closely by viewers.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 15:30:21.</i></td>', 'Outstanding clarity. Good tonal range. B&W is a good choice of presentation. You are to be commended for including very, very faint detail. Interesting way to convey the idea of darkness. The outstanding photographic quality is the strength of your image. Most viewers will understand it fits the challenge, but there will be a few that do not. The rightmost candle is a little overexposed which will hold down your score slightly. Overall this is an outstanding image that should score decently if studied closely by viewers.', '2005-06-21 10:04:48.000000', '2005-06-22 16:30:21.000000', 1),
(1470889, 190292, 36499, '<td valign="top">focus on this seems soft(maybe slight camera shake) and the rising sun has blown out detail in the clouds. the composition is good ,colors are vibrant. the best i can vote this is a 6...good luck in the challenge and i hope i helped but please remember that my only intention is to help and it is only my own personal opinion. have a great day! :o)</td>', 'focus on this seems soft(maybe slight camera shake) and the rising sun has blown out detail in the clouds. the composition is good ,colors are vibrant. the best i can vote this is a 6...good luck in the challenge and i hope i helped but please remember that my only intention is to help and it is only my own personal opinion. have a great day! :o)', '2005-06-21 10:12:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470890, 190214, 36499, '<td valign="top">i like the green color here but i would have liked to see a difference in the water from the sand. the night sky needs to be more black as it looks(on my monitor) it looks brown. brightness and contrast can fix this. good luck5</td>', 'i like the green color here but i would have liked to see a difference in the water from the sand. the night sky needs to be more black as it looks(on my monitor) it looks brown. brightness and contrast can fix this. good luck5', '2005-06-21 10:15:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470894, 187689, 5792, '<td valign="top">Sky, moon, and reflective water are good ingrediets for en evening cityscape. To have about 1/3rd of the image devoted to horizon below the sky is generally about right for a cityscape. Sunset is the gateway to darkness so fits the challenge theme well.<br/> <br/>This image will score low for several reasons. There is considerable electronic noise in the sky that should be removed. The image is very soft focused and has a yellowish hue common inn low light level situations. There should be color corrections applied in post processing to bring out latent colors and add visual interest to the image. <br/> <br/>There is not a lot appealing for viewers to see in this image. The composition lacks a central focal point that the viewer will like to look at. The building and moon ar about the only things to attract the viewers eyes and those are small with little detail to be seen.<br/> <br/>The river is calm and would make for great reflections but there is very little for it to reflect. There is plenty of sky in the composition but not much there to look at either. Good cityscapes with lighted skies like this are better if it contains clouds.</td>', 'Sky, moon, and reflective water are good ingrediets for en evening cityscape. To have about 1/3rd of the image devoted to horizon below the sky is generally about right for a cityscape. Sunset is the gateway to darkness so fits the challenge theme well. This image will score low for several reasons. There is considerable electronic noise in the sky that should be removed. The image is very soft focused and has a yellowish hue common inn low light level situations. There should be color corrections applied in post processing to bring out latent colors and add visual interest to the image.  There is not a lot appealing for viewers to see in this image. The composition lacks a central focal point that the viewer will like to look at. The building and moon ar about the only things to attract the viewers eyes and those are small with little detail to be seen. The river is calm and would make for great reflections but there is very little for it to reflect. There is plenty of sky in the composition but not much there to look at either. Good cityscapes with lighted skies like this are better if it contains clouds.', '2005-06-21 10:17:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470901, 190244, 38838, '<td valign="top">The photograph speaks volumes but (perhaps) too loudly.</td>', 'The photograph speaks volumes but (perhaps) too loudly.', '2005-06-21 10:21:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470911, 188888, 5792, '<td valign="top">Good attempt to add interest to the composition though use of perspective. This urban study peaks the interst of the viewer. The harsh lighting on the building is the strength of the composition. General photographic quality is OK.<br/> <br/>Generally speaking the two overexposed areas where the lamps are would be a photographic error but appear to support the nature of this particular composition. That will work for some viewers but not for others. Some viewers will have difficulty finding something in the composition they care much about or can relate to and will vote it lower because of it.</td>', 'Good attempt to add interest to the composition though use of perspective. This urban study peaks the interst of the viewer. The harsh lighting on the building is the strength of the composition. General photographic quality is OK. Generally speaking the two overexposed areas where the lamps are would be a photographic error but appear to support the nature of this particular composition. That will work for some viewers but not for others. Some viewers will have difficulty finding something in the composition they care much about or can relate to and will vote it lower because of it.', '2005-06-21 10:28:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470914, 189351, 39193, '<td valign="top">this is a beautiful image..both wonderful and haunting at the same time!</td>', 'this is a beautiful image..both wonderful and haunting at the same time!', '2005-06-21 10:31:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470916, 190165, 38838, '<td valign="top">Blind yet seen . . . substantial but not . . . directionless digits . . . illuminated and dark. Excellent. Bravo!</td>', 'Blind yet seen . . . substantial but not . . . directionless digits . . . illuminated and dark. Excellent. Bravo!', '2005-06-21 10:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470924, 189256, 5792, '<td valign="top">Homelessness is good darkness concept. Framing is fine. Depth of field works for the greenery behind.<br/> <br/>The softness of the image focus will result in lower scores and is its most notable defect. At this distance viewers expect to be able to see more detail in your subject, despite his condition and the nature of this shot. <br/> <br/>Overall the colors in this composition are weak, even the green in the background. Brightening the colors would add more visual interest to the composition. This could be intentional but will not work very well for most viewers.<br/> <br/>This image captured from a ''snapshoot'' angle and might be more interesting if taken from a different perspective like from below or from the level of the homeless person. This makes you look figuratively like you are looking down on the homeless though that is probably not you intention.</td>', 'Homelessness is good darkness concept. Framing is fine. Depth of field works for the greenery behind. The softness of the image focus will result in lower scores and is its most notable defect. At this distance viewers expect to be able to see more detail in your subject, despite his condition and the nature of this shot.  Overall the colors in this composition are weak, even the green in the background. Brightening the colors would add more visual interest to the composition. This could be intentional but will not work very well for most viewers. This image captured from a ''snapshoot'' angle and might be more interesting if taken from a different perspective like from below or from the level of the homeless person. This makes you look figuratively like you are looking down on the homeless though that is probably not you intention.', '2005-06-21 10:38:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470930, 190280, 38838, '<td valign="top">Scary</td>', 'Scary', '2005-06-21 10:40:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470942, 190217, 5792, '<td valign="top">Black cats fit a dark theme for this challenge. General photographic qualiity and clarity is good and the closeup composition is fine. Lighting is OK.<br/> <br/>This woud be wrong but many viewers will see this as an attempt to slip a pet picture into the challenge and vote it lower.<br/> <br/>There are a lot of white specks, particularly around the right eye, that will detract from the composition as will the out-of-place hair on the right near the whiskers. This image would score higher if those items could have been cleaned off.<br/> <br/>The image shows some digitalization ''jaggie'' effects on the cat''s whiskers. The reflection of the flash in the cat''s right eye is a slight distraction.<br/> <br/>Overall this is a well framed macro composition.</td>', 'Black cats fit a dark theme for this challenge. General photographic qualiity and clarity is good and the closeup composition is fine. Lighting is OK. This woud be wrong but many viewers will see this as an attempt to slip a pet picture into the challenge and vote it lower. There are a lot of white specks, particularly around the right eye, that will detract from the composition as will the out-of-place hair on the right near the whiskers. This image would score higher if those items could have been cleaned off. The image shows some digitalization ''jaggie'' effects on the cat''s whiskers. The reflection of the flash in the cat''s right eye is a slight distraction. Overall this is a well framed macro composition.', '2005-06-21 10:48:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470944, 187969, 38838, '<td valign="top">I like the definition of the shadow juxtaposed with the clearly visable yet slightly blurred gate and the darkness beyond it -- intangible tangibility. (A little more cropped off the right side might be in order.)</td>', 'I like the definition of the shadow juxtaposed with the clearly visable yet slightly blurred gate and the darkness beyond it -- intangible tangibility. (A little more cropped off the right side might be in order.)', '2005-06-21 10:48:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470951, 188120, 38838, '<td valign="top">Interesting lights and darks and transparents. Imaginative. Well done.</td>', 'Interesting lights and darks and transparents. Imaginative. Well done.', '2005-06-21 10:51:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470952, 190273, 5792, '<td valign="top">Marvelous composition. The framing is perfect and the grey mid-tones are very good. Just a nice capture that proves that great pictures are everywhere. B&amp;W works for this image.<br/> <br/>On the technical side the top lighted parts of the blinds are overexposed and hurts the composition slightly.<br/> <br/>This is a very goo capture and should score high.</td>', 'Marvelous composition. The framing is perfect and the grey mid-tones are very good. Just a nice capture that proves that great pictures are everywhere. B&W works for this image. On the technical side the top lighted parts of the blinds are overexposed and hurts the composition slightly. This is a very goo capture and should score high.', '2005-06-21 10:52:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470965, 188324, 38838, '<td valign="top">Is this a photograph of a living tiger or of a painting of a tiger? The definition, contrasts, and presentation are amazing.</td>', 'Is this a photograph of a living tiger or of a painting of a tiger? The definition, contrasts, and presentation are amazing.', '2005-06-21 10:59:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470975, 189224, 5792, '<td valign="top">Terrific tonal range and perspective in this B&amp;W study. Gives viewers something to think about.<br/> <br/>he technical quality of the image is outstanding even though the hair on the subject''s head appears to be soft compared to the rest of the image. Perhaps a slow shutter speed captured subject movement.<br/> <br/>Viewers will wonder about the purpose of the garment in the chair. It does not appear to serve a purpose so might be better if it were removed.<br/> <br/>The window is not level in the composition and will act as a distraction. Intentional angling should be 15 degrees or more to be effective and meaningful to most viewers. Anything close to being horizontal should be made horizontal.<br/> <br/>This is a good image that will score in the upper tier.</td>', 'Terrific tonal range and perspective in this B&W study. Gives viewers something to think about. he technical quality of the image is outstanding even though the hair on the subject''s head appears to be soft compared to the rest of the image. Perhaps a slow shutter speed captured subject movement. Viewers will wonder about the purpose of the garment in the chair. It does not appear to serve a purpose so might be better if it were removed. The window is not level in the composition and will act as a distraction. Intentional angling should be 15 degrees or more to be effective and meaningful to most viewers. Anything close to being horizontal should be made horizontal. This is a good image that will score in the upper tier.', '2005-06-21 11:02:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470977, 190232, 38869, '<td valign="top">I like the photo, it seems a bit of a stretch for the topic though.</td>', 'I like the photo, it seems a bit of a stretch for the topic though.', '2005-06-21 11:03:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1470979, 189607, 38869, '<td valign="top">Beautiful.</td>', 'Beautiful.', '2005-06-21 11:04:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471008, 188020, 5792, '<td valign="top">The idea of this image is perfect for the challenge. Including a candle and two wine glasses is good and having the waiting person softer focused in the background is good. Not showing their face works very well. That implies that it could be anyone waiting, including the viewer. The way you have framed the scene is very good.<br/> <br/>There is a lot of weakness in the quality of the photograph that prevent the viewer from realizing the full potential this image has to offer.<br/> <br/>First and foremost is focus. This is a killer! Poor focus will hurt the score of this image more than anything else. If it were done purposefully this way it will not work for most viewers. The glasses should be in sharp focus to convey the idea we are waiting for something good that the person waiting has specially prepared. It loosk like the camera is focused on the front of the table with a very shallow depth of field (DOF). The DOF may be fine but just centered in the wrong place.<br/> <br/>The candle should be placed differently with respect to the glass.  Perhaps it should be placed directly between the glasses or off to one side. In this position it distracts the viewer by being partially obscured. The candle flame is overexposed  and that acts as a major distraction.<br/> <br/>The image would work better if the amount of liquid in the glasses were different. If someone is waiting they will either drink nothing or drink from only one glass. If someone is waiting for someone then either both glasses should be full or only one glass should be less than full, but NOT both and they should definitely not both be empty by exactly the same amount.<br/> <br/>This is an image with great potential. You will do a lot better with this next time I am sure.</td>', 'The idea of this image is perfect for the challenge. Including a candle and two wine glasses is good and having the waiting person softer focused in the background is good. Not showing their face works very well. That implies that it could be anyone waiting, including the viewer. The way you have framed the scene is very good. There is a lot of weakness in the quality of the photograph that prevent the viewer from realizing the full potential this image has to offer. First and foremost is focus. This is a killer! Poor focus will hurt the score of this image more than anything else. If it were done purposefully this way it will not work for most viewers. The glasses should be in sharp focus to convey the idea we are waiting for something good that the person waiting has specially prepared. It loosk like the camera is focused on the front of the table with a very shallow depth of field (DOF). The DOF may be fine but just centered in the wrong place. The candle should be placed differently with respect to the glass.  Perhaps it should be placed directly between the glasses or off to one side. In this position it distracts the viewer by being partially obscured. The candle flame is overexposed  and that acts as a major distraction. The image would work better if the amount of liquid in the glasses were different. If someone is waiting they will either drink nothing or drink from only one glass. If someone is waiting for someone then either both glasses should be full or only one glass should be less than full, but NOT both and they should definitely not both be empty by exactly the same amount. This is an image with great potential. You will do a lot better with this next time I am sure.', '2005-06-21 11:21:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471016, 188549, 5792, '<td valign="top">Close cropped composition is OK and the idea fits the challenge well. B&amp;W is a good choice of expression for this image.<br/> <br/>There are several technical issues that will hurt it in voting.<br/> <br/>The first is focus. You probably made the child''s face soft focused on purpose but it will not work for most viewers. They will feel it is just poorly focused and not "get it". The small amount of background visible appears in clearer focus than the model and that acts as a major distraction in this composition. You will have to come up with a different way to convey the idea of dreaming.<br/> <br/>The contrast is very low in this image. Just apply an autocantrast and you will probably see a positive change. This image needs to have the black point set to give it better tonal range and contrast.</td>', 'Close cropped composition is OK and the idea fits the challenge well. B&W is a good choice of expression for this image. There are several technical issues that will hurt it in voting. The first is focus. You probably made the child''s face soft focused on purpose but it will not work for most viewers. They will feel it is just poorly focused and not "get it". The small amount of background visible appears in clearer focus than the model and that acts as a major distraction in this composition. You will have to come up with a different way to convey the idea of dreaming. The contrast is very low in this image. Just apply an autocantrast and you will probably see a positive change. This image needs to have the black point set to give it better tonal range and contrast.', '2005-06-21 11:29:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471025, 187305, 5792, '<td valign="top">Composition is fine. The lighting from above is particularly good.<br/> <br/>You are probably aware you will be criticized for entering a flower image in a darkness challenge and should expect a low score. A black background is not enough to sway the feelings of many DPC voters.<br/> <br/>The hallmark of a good floral macro is focus. In most cases it should be in razor sharp focus or (in challenges that allow it) be processed with filters for a softer and more surrealistic look. This macro is not sharp enough to work well.<br/> <br/>The color is a little weak. You might consider color processing to bring out more red and yellow to increase eye appeal.</td>', 'Composition is fine. The lighting from above is particularly good. You are probably aware you will be criticized for entering a flower image in a darkness challenge and should expect a low score. A black background is not enough to sway the feelings of many DPC voters. The hallmark of a good floral macro is focus. In most cases it should be in razor sharp focus or (in challenges that allow it) be processed with filters for a softer and more surrealistic look. This macro is not sharp enough to work well. The color is a little weak. You might consider color processing to bring out more red and yellow to increase eye appeal.', '2005-06-21 11:35:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471037, 189420, 5792, '<td valign="top">An interesting concept in this composition. The exposure seems OK.<br/> <br/>Like in most images focus is the most fundamental characteristic to get right. Most viewers will feel this image should be in sharper focus and vote it lower.<br/> <br/>Many low light level images have a yellow hue like this. It is because the camera''s white balence gets fooled under these conditions. Then you have to do color adjustment to make the lighting ''correct''. Viewers will see that as a defect in this image even if the lighting is right.<br/> <br/>You might consider positioning the lights diagonally for added viewer interest.</td>', 'An interesting concept in this composition. The exposure seems OK. Like in most images focus is the most fundamental characteristic to get right. Most viewers will feel this image should be in sharper focus and vote it lower. Many low light level images have a yellow hue like this. It is because the camera''s white balence gets fooled under these conditions. Then you have to do color adjustment to make the lighting ''correct''. Viewers will see that as a defect in this image even if the lighting is right. You might consider positioning the lights diagonally for added viewer interest.', '2005-06-21 11:42:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471050, 188235, 14986, '<td valign="top"><br/>Technically,  I see a few issues.  Pretty evident haloing around the steeple and cross.   It seems the picture quality is a bit low, with the steeple and cross not being very clearly edged and just a general lack of detail.  I like the composition, although I might have preferred the cross at a slightly more "straight on" angle.  <br/> <br/>As far as the message of the photo ,  [climbing up on soapbox]   There certainly is a side to "religion" that can be considered dark.   It does seem like Christianity takes a lot of abuse...as you don''t see the icons, holy items or sacred words of other religions  singled out as often for negativity.... and if it does happen there''s usually an uproar about being non tolerant of other faiths.     A lot of good has been done in the name of religion as well.   Anytime you get folks feeling very strongly one way or another about an issue, you will see extremes in actions as well.    Even Jesus pointed out how dangerous it is to focus on the "doing" of religion, vs. actually living a life of faith.     [stepping down from soapbox]<br/> <br/>I would not have used this message, but I understand it.   Although I am a Christian, be assured that I have not lowered your score because of it.</td>', 'Technically,  I see a few issues.  Pretty evident haloing around the steeple and cross.   It seems the picture quality is a bit low, with the steeple and cross not being very clearly edged and just a general lack of detail.  I like the composition, although I might have preferred the cross at a slightly more "straight on" angle.   As far as the message of the photo ,  [climbing up on soapbox]   There certainly is a side to "religion" that can be considered dark.   It does seem like Christianity takes a lot of abuse...as you don''t see the icons, holy items or sacred words of other religions  singled out as often for negativity.... and if it does happen there''s usually an uproar about being non tolerant of other faiths.     A lot of good has been done in the name of religion as well.   Anytime you get folks feeling very strongly one way or another about an issue, you will see extremes in actions as well.    Even Jesus pointed out how dangerous it is to focus on the "doing" of religion, vs. actually living a life of faith.     [stepping down from soapbox] I would not have used this message, but I understand it.   Although I am a Christian, be assured that I have not lowered your score because of it.', '2005-06-21 11:49:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471061, 187192, 12051, '<td valign="top">I like the photo. I just don''t see the connection with darkness?</td>', 'I like the photo. I just don''t see the connection with darkness?', '2005-06-21 11:53:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1471063, 190186, 5792, '<td valign="top">This is the classic modern day misunderstood youth image. Use of B&amp;W and high grain is proper in this context. It fits the challenge topic well. It is well composed and you have captured a great expression. It has a nice soid black and the tonal range is very good.<br/> <br/>The score received is generally related to the connection the average viewer makes with the subject. They do not have to like the subject but they do have to find a basis of understanding. The rebelliosness of youth will not be enough for most DPCers to relate to this image. You probably accept that and don''t expect it to get a high score.<br/> <br/>On the technical side the image has a number of white specks in the black background that are distracting and should be removed. You might have considered shifting the camera more to the right so that both hands show complete in the frame. That would give the image better balence. <br/> <br/>Overall this is a good picture.</td>', 'This is the classic modern day misunderstood youth image. Use of B&W and high grain is proper in this context. It fits the challenge topic well. It is well composed and you have captured a great expression. It has a nice soid black and the tonal range is very good. The score received is generally related to the connection the average viewer makes with the subject. They do not have to like the subject but they do have to find a basis of understanding. The rebelliosness of youth will not be enough for most DPCers to relate to this image. You probably accept that and don''t expect it to get a high score. On the technical side the image has a number of white specks in the black background that are distracting and should be removed. You might have considered shifting the camera more to the right so that both hands show complete in the frame. That would give the image better balence.  Overall this is a good picture.', '2005-06-21 11:54:29.000000', NULL, 1),
