(1473691, 187294, 27851, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skylen:</b></div><hr/><i> Wow, please tell us how you executed this shot. What is the lighting, is it flash? Is it really shot at 1/1000 sec f/8 ISO64??? That seems like a really low exposure for anything but a powerful flash, and I didn''t know the F828 could sync with flash at such a high shutter speed.<br/> <br/>I''m still blown away and I wish I could make images like this. Awesome. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>upto 1/3200 , i use Metz mecablitz 54 MZ-4 with both my cameras :)<br/> <br/>*also i used á wide angle conversion lens 180° from Bowens... :P<br/> <br/>thx. all 5´th place is excellent for this pic.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 06:45:17.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by skylen: Wow, please tell us how you executed this shot. What is the lighting, is it flash? Is it really shot at 1/1000 sec f/8 ISO64??? That seems like a really low exposure for anything but a powerful flash, and I didn''t know the F828 could sync with flash at such a high shutter speed. I''m still blown away and I wish I could make images like this. Awesome.   upto 1/3200 , i use Metz mecablitz 54 MZ-4 with both my cameras :) *also i used á wide angle conversion lens 180° from Bowens... :P thx. all 5´th place is excellent for this pic.', '2005-06-22 07:44:03.000000', '2005-06-22 07:45:17.000000', 0),
(1473716, 190182, 21540, '<td valign="top">Thanks all for your comment.<br/> <br/>Regarding Arngrimur´s picture The Mystic River who got the blue ribon in the Beauty challange.  I had never seen that picture before.  I posted my picture on an Icelandic photo website and Smali pointed out to me that my picture would be grate for the Darkness challange. You can take a look at that forum and there you can see it for your self and since you are also Icelandic you can  understand what people are saying.<br/><a href="//www.ljosmyndakeppni.is/viewtopic.php?t=2421" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.ljosmyndakeppni.is/viewtopic.php?t=2421</a> <br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks all for your comment. Regarding Arngrimur´s picture The Mystic River who got the blue ribon in the Beauty challange.  I had never seen that picture before.  I posted my picture on an Icelandic photo website and Smali pointed out to me that my picture would be grate for the Darkness challange. You can take a look at that forum and there you can see it for your self and since you are also Icelandic you can  understand what people are saying.//www.ljosmyndakeppni.is/viewtopic.php?t=2421  ', '2005-06-22 07:55:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(1473735, 189943, 36981, '<td valign="top">Many thanks for those who commented on this photo.  It was fun to read what you had to say.<br/> <br/>This is a cave facing the Mediteranean in the south of France.  It is not, unfortunately, my own.  We were vacationing there and I saw the cave &amp; bed from a peddle boat I was on with my family.  I made them go back the next day to photograph it, but there were 8 foot swells, so I''m afraid it wasn''t quite as crisp as I''d have liked.<br/> <br/>Again, thanks for voting &amp; commenting!</td>', 'Many thanks for those who commented on this photo.  It was fun to read what you had to say. This is a cave facing the Mediteranean in the south of France.  It is not, unfortunately, my own.  We were vacationing there and I saw the cave & bed from a peddle boat I was on with my family.  I made them go back the next day to photograph it, but there were 8 foot swells, so I''m afraid it wasn''t quite as crisp as I''d have liked. Again, thanks for voting & commenting!', '2005-06-22 08:00:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(1473838, 188112, 37544, '<td valign="top">I expected it to do alot better myself until I uploaded it.  In the original the eyes were still blue but not overdone looking.  Uploading problems I guess? Maybe when I resized it? This is a picture I took of my son and me. He always gives me a great pose! I switched the photo to black and white, then infared, then blue tint... and POOF--FREAK SHOW DROP-OUT! Oh well, it was fun and my son thinks that it is "the coolest picture ever!"</td>', 'I expected it to do alot better myself until I uploaded it.  In the original the eyes were still blue but not overdone looking.  Uploading problems I guess? Maybe when I resized it? This is a picture I took of my son and me. He always gives me a great pose! I switched the photo to black and white, then infared, then blue tint... and POOF--FREAK SHOW DROP-OUT! Oh well, it was fun and my son thinks that it is "the coolest picture ever!"', '2005-06-22 08:50:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1473846, 189256, 37298, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the feedback.<br/> <br/>Some of you addressed the "softness" of the photo. The sharpness seems to have been lost when I scaled it down for submission. The photo was very sharp and crisp.<br/> <br/><a href="//photobucket.com/albums/y271/greenberg_k9/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Other pictures of mine</a></td>', 'Thanks for all the feedback. Some of you addressed the "softness" of the photo. The sharpness seems to have been lost when I scaled it down for submission. The photo was very sharp and crisp. Other pictures of mine', '2005-06-22 08:53:00.000000', NULL, 0),
