(1474166, 190213, 16053, '<td valign="top">One comment to some of the posts: there''s a fuzzy aspect on the green light/smoke in the low right. I think it was because of too much sharpness. I sharpened it before the crop and resize and after resize. I think this is why there''s a bit of halo around the subject and the dot aspect of the low right smoke.</td>', 'One comment to some of the posts: there''s a fuzzy aspect on the green light/smoke in the low right. I think it was because of too much sharpness. I sharpened it before the crop and resize and after resize. I think this is why there''s a bit of halo around the subject and the dot aspect of the low right smoke.', '2005-06-22 10:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474177, 190314, 36231, '<td valign="top">This was hard on my eyes because it looked upside down. I hope you don''t mind, I copied it and rotated it:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=194185" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36231/thumb/194185.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36231/thumb/194185.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/36231/thumb/194185.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>It helps the photo alot.  Also, check out this tutorial, as it helped me out tremendously. :)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/tutorial.php?TUTORIAL_ID=26" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Using PhotoShop to Prepare Photos for DPC</a></td>', 'This was hard on my eyes because it looked upside down. I hope you don''t mind, I copied it and rotated it:   It helps the photo alot.  Also, check out this tutorial, as it helped me out tremendously. :) Using PhotoShop to Prepare Photos for DPC', '2005-06-22 10:21:09.000000', NULL, 0),
