(1474551, 190285, 30817, '<td valign="top">While most your peers are primarily into clothing with merely an acquiesent nod to their environment, you are capturing and interpreting it with a camera in your hands.  I bow to you, young lady, remembering the name Anna Holdhazy as belonging to one that will someday impact the photographic art community, if that is your deep desire.</td>', 'While most your peers are primarily into clothing with merely an acquiesent nod to their environment, you are capturing and interpreting it with a camera in your hands.  I bow to you, young lady, remembering the name Anna Holdhazy as belonging to one that will someday impact the photographic art community, if that is your deep desire.', '2005-06-22 11:42:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474572, 190139, 22872, '<td valign="top">What a sweet beautiful face......and they grow up so fast! :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'What a sweet beautiful face......and they grow up so fast! :) ', '2005-06-22 11:45:36.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474580, 190015, 22872, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote this round but when I saw this picture I thought the puppy has her eyes squinted...I didn''t realize she was blind!  Poor baby...pretty amazing how they adapt.  I have 2 weiner dogs...one from a wiener dog rescue group (she''s extremely highstrung and was severely abused) and my second from the dogpound and he loves everybody!  I''m always glad to see someone that adopts from rescue groups :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'I didn''t vote this round but when I saw this picture I thought the puppy has her eyes squinted...I didn''t realize she was blind!  Poor baby...pretty amazing how they adapt.  I have 2 weiner dogs...one from a wiener dog rescue group (she''s extremely highstrung and was severely abused) and my second from the dogpound and he loves everybody!  I''m always glad to see someone that adopts from rescue groups :) ', '2005-06-22 11:47:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474595, 189351, 1717, '<td valign="top">love this...great work!  should have ribboned.</td>', 'love this...great work!  should have ribboned.', '2005-06-22 11:50:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474620, 187746, 22872, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote this round but wanted to come back to see how this photo did.  I know when I saw it as a thumbnail I thought someone had did the ''black'' photo thing...but once I opened it (at home on laptop) I could faintly see the nose...then the chin.  I''m at work now and I have a LCD flatscreen with a privacy screen and I am almost unable to make it out...this may be what happened with the voters....they probably didn''t see it.  I just wanted to let you know I thought it was a very cool picture :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'I didn''t vote this round but wanted to come back to see how this photo did.  I know when I saw it as a thumbnail I thought someone had did the ''black'' photo thing...but once I opened it (at home on laptop) I could faintly see the nose...then the chin.  I''m at work now and I have a LCD flatscreen with a privacy screen and I am almost unable to make it out...this may be what happened with the voters....they probably didn''t see it.  I just wanted to let you know I thought it was a very cool picture :) ', '2005-06-22 11:55:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474726, 190165, 34659, '<td valign="top">I felt sure that this was your work Nico...  And as usual, I thought it was flawless (10)!  I had this one picked to ribbon for sure - sorry that it didn''t finish higher, but top 20 ain''t bad out of 364!<br/> <br/>Congrats again on a beautiful &amp; powerful image.  I''m sure we''ll continue to see great things from you!<br/> <br/>Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/>Jimmy<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 11:30:20.</i></td>', 'I felt sure that this was your work Nico...  And as usual, I thought it was flawless (10)!  I had this one picked to ribbon for sure - sorry that it didn''t finish higher, but top 20 ain''t bad out of 364! Congrats again on a beautiful & powerful image.  I''m sure we''ll continue to see great things from you! Just my 2 cents... Jimmy', '2005-06-22 12:29:56.000000', '2005-06-22 12:30:20.000000', 0),
(1474754, 189353, 35804, '<td valign="top">for me...darkness is not all things morbid and depressing or creepy and weird...I find a certain comfort in it''s coolness...a safety in it''s shelter...a beauty in it''s softness...and perhaps I''m a little old fashioned...but keeping the hot sunshine out of my house during these hot southern summers really helps with the energy bills...really...it does...don''t hate me because I''m frugal   :P<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 11:43:29.</i></td>', 'for me...darkness is not all things morbid and depressing or creepy and weird...I find a certain comfort in it''s coolness...a safety in it''s shelter...a beauty in it''s softness...and perhaps I''m a little old fashioned...but keeping the hot sunshine out of my house during these hot southern summers really helps with the energy bills...really...it does...don''t hate me because I''m frugal   :P', '2005-06-22 12:37:21.000000', '2005-06-22 12:43:29.000000', 0),
(1474764, 187294, 31533, '<td valign="top">Great photo but I don''t think spot editing is allowed in basic rules.</td>', 'Great photo but I don''t think spot editing is allowed in basic rules.', '2005-06-22 12:39:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474838, 189281, 30817, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Falc:</b></div><hr/><i> size matters </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>... only when you have no furthering merits.  Only then.  This photograph was, I am convinced, prejudged and probably not even studied by many who summarily looked for a reason to degrade. How like life is photography.<br/> <br/>gwyndbartlett, you made a tender photograph that deserved better reception.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 11:58:38.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Falc: size matters   ... only when you have no furthering merits.  Only then.  This photograph was, I am convinced, prejudged and probably not even studied by many who summarily looked for a reason to degrade. How like life is photography. gwyndbartlett, you made a tender photograph that deserved better reception.', '2005-06-22 12:57:45.000000', '2005-06-22 12:58:38.000000', 0),
(1474875, 189355, 21915, '<td valign="top">Thanks everyone for voting :-)</td>', 'Thanks everyone for voting :-)', '2005-06-22 13:07:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474884, 189462, 39217, '<td valign="top">Thanks Jutilda, graphicfunk and Xilebo<br/> <br/>..takk fyrir það Xilebo, þú ert aldeilis búinn að gera það gott hér 2 borðar það er meiriháttar.<br/>-HKH</td>', 'Thanks Jutilda, graphicfunk and Xilebo ..takk fyrir það Xilebo, þú ert aldeilis búinn að gera það gott hér 2 borðar það er meiriháttar.-HKH', '2005-06-22 13:08:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1474914, 189599, 14603, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SJCarter:</b></div><hr/><i> Can''t believe this didn''t ribbon...  IMHO, this was easily the best shot in the challenge.  Fantastic work - man!  Everything about it is just superb. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Can`t argue with that...great shot with so much going on.</td>', 'Originally posted by SJCarter: Can''t believe this didn''t ribbon...  IMHO, this was easily the best shot in the challenge.  Fantastic work - man!  Everything about it is just superb.   Can`t argue with that...great shot with so much going on.', '2005-06-22 13:15:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475016, 187646, 19025, '<td valign="top">I thought this would do better than it did. Oh well, someday, someway, I''ll get to that top 10..I''m determined!!</td>', 'I thought this would do better than it did. Oh well, someday, someway, I''ll get to that top 10..I''m determined!!', '2005-06-22 13:35:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475056, 187294, 27851, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Tom_Robbrecht:</b></div><hr/><i> Great photo but I don''t think spot editing is allowed in basic rules. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>no spot edit actually complete layer effect over whole image only. .. find out later after proffness test ;)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Tom_Robbrecht: Great photo but I don''t think spot editing is allowed in basic rules.  no spot edit actually complete layer effect over whole image only. .. find out later after proffness test ;)', '2005-06-22 13:43:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475064, 189607, 32792, '<td valign="top">HAHAH, this is no longer zoomdak''s "private spot".<br/>I was 100% sure this was his shot, but then what a surprise! It''s novatiger''s shot! Oh well, with such an incredible place, shooting this is even more than a pleasure, it''s a blessing! Great work and congrats<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 12:45:54.</i></td>', 'HAHAH, this is no longer zoomdak''s "private spot".I was 100% sure this was his shot, but then what a surprise! It''s novatiger''s shot! Oh well, with such an incredible place, shooting this is even more than a pleasure, it''s a blessing! Great work and congrats', '2005-06-22 13:45:26.000000', '2005-06-22 13:45:54.000000', 0);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(1475164, 187002, 24951, '<td valign="top">Yes I see the eye and eyebrow and forehead (including crease). Skin is very dark gray.</td>', 'Yes I see the eye and eyebrow and forehead (including crease). Skin is very dark gray.', '2005-06-22 14:07:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475171, 189234, 20577, '<td valign="top">How did this end up way down here?</td>', 'How did this end up way down here?', '2005-06-22 14:09:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475227, 188296, 32754, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, was my top pick..felt it belonged in top 5.</td>', 'Congratulations, was my top pick..felt it belonged in top 5.', '2005-06-22 14:24:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475237, 190231, 14858, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone who took the time to leave a comment!<br/> <br/>I''m very pleased with how the shot turned out, this is my best finish in a Challenge to date.  The shot itself was a (hopefully not) "Once in a Lifetime" capture for me, and I''m just glad I was lucky enough to be in the right place at the right time.<br/> <br/>For those who were wondering where the "Darkness" element was in the shot, If you''ve ever been alone in the wilderness under a moonless night sky, with a lantern as your only source of light.  You''ll know exactly the feeling invoked by a gradually dimming, and ultimately "Dark Lantern".  When the only sense of your surroundings is revealed to you in momentary flashes by the approaching storm.<br/> <br/>That is what "Darkness" means to me.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for all the kind words!<br/> <br/>Bill</td>', 'Thanks to everyone who took the time to leave a comment! I''m very pleased with how the shot turned out, this is my best finish in a Challenge to date.  The shot itself was a (hopefully not) "Once in a Lifetime" capture for me, and I''m just glad I was lucky enough to be in the right place at the right time. For those who were wondering where the "Darkness" element was in the shot, If you''ve ever been alone in the wilderness under a moonless night sky, with a lantern as your only source of light.  You''ll know exactly the feeling invoked by a gradually dimming, and ultimately "Dark Lantern".  When the only sense of your surroundings is revealed to you in momentary flashes by the approaching storm. That is what "Darkness" means to me. Thanks again for all the kind words! Bill', '2005-06-22 14:27:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475245, 190166, 32754, '<td valign="top">34th..not bad, however, I thought it would be in top 20..very powerful shot.</td>', '34th..not bad, however, I thought it would be in top 20..very powerful shot.', '2005-06-22 14:29:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475311, 190166, 28742, '<td valign="top">A great image for the challenge! A good finish as well. Good thing you included the word "abandoned" in the description. ;-)</td>', 'A great image for the challenge! A good finish as well. Good thing you included the word "abandoned" in the description. ;-)', '2005-06-22 14:50:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475349, 189732, 31409, '<td valign="top">I enjoyed this picture in the challenge, and forgot to look at the surroundings. :-p<br/> <br/>Lucky you didn''t have the bucket placed in front of him.</td>', 'I enjoyed this picture in the challenge, and forgot to look at the surroundings. :-p Lucky you didn''t have the bucket placed in front of him.', '2005-06-22 14:57:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475365, 187730, 20941, '<td valign="top">congratulations on your Ribbon with this awesome shot! Great Work!</td>', 'congratulations on your Ribbon with this awesome shot! Great Work!', '2005-06-22 15:02:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475372, 189603, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your Red with this wonderful image so well suited to this challenge!</td>', 'Congratulations on your Red with this wonderful image so well suited to this challenge!', '2005-06-22 15:03:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475377, 189607, 20941, '<td valign="top">Congratulations o0n your Blue with this stunning shot! Beautiful work!</td>', 'Congratulations o0n your Blue with this stunning shot! Beautiful work!', '2005-06-22 15:05:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475382, 189603, 15919, '<td valign="top">Congrats, deserved ribbon<br/> <br/>Til hamingju.  Helv..... töff mynd.</td>', 'Congrats, deserved ribbon Til hamingju.  Helv..... töff mynd.', '2005-06-22 15:06:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475395, 188296, 34247, '<td valign="top">Very nice shot, and a good choice for b/w usage. I feel though that this would be more effective with a stronger light source coming in through the slit. Perhaps a higher contrast value. Perhaps a closer crop to the head area. As it is, the impact of the light dissipates towards the left side of the frame, and I feel the drama factor is lost a bit on that negative space. Personally, I''d have gone for a square crop of the head and the slit.</td>', 'Very nice shot, and a good choice for b/w usage. I feel though that this would be more effective with a stronger light source coming in through the slit. Perhaps a higher contrast value. Perhaps a closer crop to the head area. As it is, the impact of the light dissipates towards the left side of the frame, and I feel the drama factor is lost a bit on that negative space. Personally, I''d have gone for a square crop of the head and the slit.', '2005-06-22 15:08:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475496, 187746, 16046, '<td valign="top">Nice work, perfect on my monitor, not your fault for the low placing. Keep it up.<br/> <br/>Frank</td>', 'Nice work, perfect on my monitor, not your fault for the low placing. Keep it up. Frank', '2005-06-22 15:29:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475497, 187296, 39221, '<td valign="top">gave 10 here too - this image is awesome</td>', 'gave 10 here too - this image is awesome', '2005-06-22 15:29:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475540, 189732, 35357, '<td valign="top">Well, at least nine people besides myself thought this was worth a 10.</td>', 'Well, at least nine people besides myself thought this was worth a 10.', '2005-06-22 15:45:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475541, 189774, 35357, '<td valign="top">This is definitely one of the top three photos of this challenge, people are insane to have scored it where it ended up! &gt;:-{</td>', 'This is definitely one of the top three photos of this challenge, people are insane to have scored it where it ended up! >:-{', '2005-06-22 15:47:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475546, 189732, 36499, '<td valign="top">i thought for sure this would finish in the top 50! i thought it was well worth the 10 i voted it. u were so robbed here..wish more voters had an open mind.</td>', 'i thought for sure this would finish in the top 50! i thought it was well worth the 10 i voted it. u were so robbed here..wish more voters had an open mind.', '2005-06-22 15:49:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475609, 187730, 20539, '<td valign="top">good job man. impressive</td>', 'good job man. impressive', '2005-06-22 16:19:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475620, 190279, 27373, '<td valign="top">I love the fact that you found "idkwthyattah" helpful.  I also love that you got more 4''s than 3''s and 2'' combined for a photo you didn''t even mean to enter.  My laugh for today!</td>', 'I love the fact that you found "idkwthyattah" helpful.  I also love that you got more 4''s than 3''s and 2'' combined for a photo you didn''t even mean to enter.  My laugh for today!', '2005-06-22 16:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475621, 190061, 30214, '<td valign="top">It takes a great vision to take a photo at daylight (and a dull daylight at that!) and to see in it potential for create a gem like this. Congrats on a great image and a good finish (could''ve been higher IMO).</td>', 'It takes a great vision to take a photo at daylight (and a dull daylight at that!) and to see in it potential for create a gem like this. Congrats on a great image and a good finish (could''ve been higher IMO).', '2005-06-22 16:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475635, 188296, 38223, '<td valign="top">Love it. It actually has something to do with the challenge description. Somehow missed this one in the vote. Would have given it a 8-9 because: beautiful lighting, well balanced cropping and simply the "professionality" feel.<br/> <br/>I maybe would have compressed the image less. There''s some slight posterisation in the back of the head.<br/> <br/>Otherwise, it is an awesome photo</td>', 'Love it. It actually has something to do with the challenge description. Somehow missed this one in the vote. Would have given it a 8-9 because: beautiful lighting, well balanced cropping and simply the "professionality" feel. I maybe would have compressed the image less. There''s some slight posterisation in the back of the head. Otherwise, it is an awesome photo', '2005-06-22 16:28:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475636, 189549, 31813, '<td valign="top">Great photo and way underrated.  <br/> <br/>I am amazed by the disparity between the average score of the commenters compared with the other voters as well as the disparity between the no-camera voters and the camera voters.    <br/> <br/>Again, great photo and it should be higher than the 31 percentile.  <br/> <br/>JV</td>', 'Great photo and way underrated.   I am amazed by the disparity between the average score of the commenters compared with the other voters as well as the disparity between the no-camera voters and the camera voters.     Again, great photo and it should be higher than the 31 percentile.   JV', '2005-06-22 16:29:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475653, 188296, 7531, '<td valign="top">It''s a terrific shot, with conotations that could go well beyond the realms of DPC. It''s stark and interesting and intense, consider a nice large blow up. Well Done!</td>', 'It''s a terrific shot, with conotations that could go well beyond the realms of DPC. It''s stark and interesting and intense, consider a nice large blow up. Well Done!', '2005-06-22 16:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475686, 190314, 35135, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments.  I took the picture much larger, but I thought that the rules called for the smaller size.  I may have misread them.  I also don''t know what that glare on the head is.  The lights were out in the room.  It may be from the light in the other room.  I didn''t think it would leave a glare, but there it is.  I like the way it looks after LadeeM rotated it as well.  It adds a lot to the composition I think.<br/> <br/>I wish I could have gotten the whole snake in the photo, she was about 2 feet long.  But she was stretched out and she would have looked too small in the shot.</td>', 'Thanks for the comments.  I took the picture much larger, but I thought that the rules called for the smaller size.  I may have misread them.  I also don''t know what that glare on the head is.  The lights were out in the room.  It may be from the light in the other room.  I didn''t think it would leave a glare, but there it is.  I like the way it looks after LadeeM rotated it as well.  It adds a lot to the composition I think. I wish I could have gotten the whole snake in the photo, she was about 2 feet long.  But she was stretched out and she would have looked too small in the shot.', '2005-06-22 16:46:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475732, 187475, 32338, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your ''Photographer''s Comments'' explanation of the technical side of your photo.  I am even more impressed with your work now.</td>', 'Thanks for your ''Photographer''s Comments'' explanation of the technical side of your photo.  I am even more impressed with your work now.', '2005-06-22 16:58:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475852, 189115, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LadeeM:</b></div><hr/><i> I gave this a low score (higher than your average, tho), mainly because I didn''t get it.  I thought it was a child "headed home".  I did get the feeling of poverty, which I connected to the darkness theme.  I can imagine it''s hard to get a photo of a homeless person.  Alone, it''s a good photo, but coupled with the other dark photos of this challenge, it didn''t really stand out much.  However, I think it deserved better than a 3.8.  That''s just silly! :) </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Thanks. I thought that one patch of darkness, especially with that bright line leading straight to it, would be enough "physical darkness" to qualify.<br/> <br/>The far more important connection to the topic is the metaphorical one, that in the richest and most powerful country in the world, able-bodied men are reduced to sleeping under freeways. The houses up the street, less than 100 feet away, are selling for over a half-million dollars.</td>', 'Originally posted by LadeeM: I gave this a low score (higher than your average, tho), mainly because I didn''t get it.  I thought it was a child "headed home".  I did get the feeling of poverty, which I connected to the darkness theme.  I can imagine it''s hard to get a photo of a homeless person.  Alone, it''s a good photo, but coupled with the other dark photos of this challenge, it didn''t really stand out much.  However, I think it deserved better than a 3.8.  That''s just silly! :)  Thanks. I thought that one patch of darkness, especially with that bright line leading straight to it, would be enough "physical darkness" to qualify. The far more important connection to the topic is the metaphorical one, that in the richest and most powerful country in the world, able-bodied men are reduced to sleeping under freeways. The houses up the street, less than 100 feet away, are selling for over a half-million dollars.', '2005-06-22 17:28:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475883, 188296, 16739, '<td valign="top">this is one of my favortes</td>', 'this is one of my favortes', '2005-06-22 17:38:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475887, 190231, 16739, '<td valign="top">nothing else to say but wow</td>', 'nothing else to say but wow', '2005-06-22 17:39:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475889, 187617, 16739, '<td valign="top">really nice shot , very clear</td>', 'really nice shot , very clear', '2005-06-22 17:39:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475895, 189956, 16739, '<td valign="top">love it ,  great shot</td>', 'love it ,  great shot', '2005-06-22 17:40:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475899, 190247, 16739, '<td valign="top">great job , very nice shot</td>', 'great job , very nice shot', '2005-06-22 17:42:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(1475903, 187730, 24454, '<td valign="top">Thanks for telling us how you did this!   It is TRULY an amazing photo!   Very desrving of a ribbon!   I think all 3 of these ribbons deserve to be blue  :)<br/> <br/>Congratulations!!<br/>SandyP<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for telling us how you did this!   It is TRULY an amazing photo!   Very desrving of a ribbon!   I think all 3 of these ribbons deserve to be blue  :) Congratulations!!SandyP ', '2005-06-22 17:43:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476033, 188296, 27373, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot.  My first instinct is to say move your subject to the left, but my first instinct is wrong.  I love the feeling of emptiness in the black and the washed out white through the gap.  I didn''t get the time to vote in this challenge (not enough to be fair at least) I probably would have given this at least an 8 and probably a 9.  I think you really captured the mood you were going for.</td>', 'I really like this shot.  My first instinct is to say move your subject to the left, but my first instinct is wrong.  I love the feeling of emptiness in the black and the washed out white through the gap.  I didn''t get the time to vote in this challenge (not enough to be fair at least) I probably would have given this at least an 8 and probably a 9.  I think you really captured the mood you were going for.', '2005-06-22 18:07:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476106, 188296, 3087, '<td valign="top">I like the shot a lot but since you asked in forums for negative reactions, I''ll give you my main niggle - the glowing of his eye - it makes this creepy in a sci-fi way rather than ominous in a more unsettling way. Other than that I think it''s excellent - the unusual compositional placement makes it feel off-balance which is perfect for the subject matter. The subtle lighting lets most of the subject remain in shadow, adding greatly to the atmosphere created and the enigmatic nature of the image.<br/> <br/>PS I didn''t vote but would have given a 7 or thereabouts, so am not one of those you were seeking when soliciting opinions. However since I had a negative reaction to offer to one small aspect, I thought I''d post.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 17:22:23.</i></td>', 'I like the shot a lot but since you asked in forums for negative reactions, I''ll give you my main niggle - the glowing of his eye - it makes this creepy in a sci-fi way rather than ominous in a more unsettling way. Other than that I think it''s excellent - the unusual compositional placement makes it feel off-balance which is perfect for the subject matter. The subtle lighting lets most of the subject remain in shadow, adding greatly to the atmosphere created and the enigmatic nature of the image. PS I didn''t vote but would have given a 7 or thereabouts, so am not one of those you were seeking when soliciting opinions. However since I had a negative reaction to offer to one small aspect, I thought I''d post.', '2005-06-22 18:21:21.000000', '2005-06-22 18:22:23.000000', 0),
(1476131, 188689, 18080, '<td valign="top">You get the lucky 1000th comment.<br/> <br/>I like this shot and gave it a 7<br/>my main critisism is that the foreground is a little busy. If you could have got a little lower and put your subject higher up the sky line in my humble opinion this would have made this shot much better. The sky has some lovely colours, and you have managed to bring them out really well with little editing. The birds in the sea add a little interest to the shot but i wouldn''t say they were essential. Horizon is nice and level and the angle of the shoreline takes you through the picture.<br/>Overall a very nice job and probably deserved to place higher than it did.<br/>Good luck with all your future challenges, and i look forward to you becoming a member in the future.<br/> <br/>Kevin</td>', 'You get the lucky 1000th comment. I like this shot and gave it a 7my main critisism is that the foreground is a little busy. If you could have got a little lower and put your subject higher up the sky line in my humble opinion this would have made this shot much better. The sky has some lovely colours, and you have managed to bring them out really well with little editing. The birds in the sea add a little interest to the shot but i wouldn''t say they were essential. Horizon is nice and level and the angle of the shoreline takes you through the picture.Overall a very nice job and probably deserved to place higher than it did.Good luck with all your future challenges, and i look forward to you becoming a member in the future. Kevin', '2005-06-22 18:26:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476141, 187294, 24976, '<td valign="top">very moody, congrats on the 5th place!</td>', 'very moody, congrats on the 5th place!', '2005-06-22 18:27:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476144, 190061, 24976, '<td valign="top">congrats on the top 10 with this exceptional photo!</td>', 'congrats on the top 10 with this exceptional photo!', '2005-06-22 18:29:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476217, 188296, 22459, '<td valign="top">I voted this image a six and feel that you have a very good capture that suits the challenge perfectly but it was just a few little aspects that could have given this image that "wow" factor to get you a ribbon.<br/>Firstly the amount of negative space is not a real issue with me and infact helps the balance, emotion and composition but the average voter here will only see it as blackness.This could have been compensated if a little more soft light could have been shed on the subject maybe from below.<br/>Regarding the subject(prisoner)if you were able to get more of a slight profile angle rather then from behind you would have been able to capture more emotion in the his face also to add more drama it would have been improved if the subject looked harder or more criminal eg tattooed skin, beard or a scar.<br/>Another little nit-pick is the eye level seems to be above the opening giving the impression that he is looking down I think this could have been improved by being level or perhaps even slightly below.<br/>A top ten finish in this very hard challenge is a great effort and my critique is just my own personel feelings on this image. <br/></td>', 'I voted this image a six and feel that you have a very good capture that suits the challenge perfectly but it was just a few little aspects that could have given this image that "wow" factor to get you a ribbon.Firstly the amount of negative space is not a real issue with me and infact helps the balance, emotion and composition but the average voter here will only see it as blackness.This could have been compensated if a little more soft light could have been shed on the subject maybe from below.Regarding the subject(prisoner)if you were able to get more of a slight profile angle rather then from behind you would have been able to capture more emotion in the his face also to add more drama it would have been improved if the subject looked harder or more criminal eg tattooed skin, beard or a scar.Another little nit-pick is the eye level seems to be above the opening giving the impression that he is looking down I think this could have been improved by being level or perhaps even slightly below.A top ten finish in this very hard challenge is a great effort and my critique is just my own personel feelings on this image. ', '2005-06-22 18:45:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1476385, 190166, 34659, '<td valign="top">A beautifully composed and executed shot.  I scored it an 8.  I think I only took off for the lighting - as I would have preferred more darkness and more of a spotlight on her, with the same composition &amp; crop.  Still, a VERY effective and emotional image that perfectly met the challenge.  Great work!<br/> <br/>I just want to add that I think your choice of models REALLY added to the human aspect of the image.  Because she is not some impossibly waifish, silicone implanted model, her (I must say, absolutely beautiful) body added an element to the shot that the majority of people can identify with more fully.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-06-22 18:29:12.</i></td>', 'A beautifully composed and executed shot.  I scored it an 8.  I think I only took off for the lighting - as I would have preferred more darkness and more of a spotlight on her, with the same composition & crop.  Still, a VERY effective and emotional image that perfectly met the challenge.  Great work! I just want to add that I think your choice of models REALLY added to the human aspect of the image.  Because she is not some impossibly waifish, silicone implanted model, her (I must say, absolutely beautiful) body added an element to the shot that the majority of people can identify with more fully.', '2005-06-22 19:26:58.000000', '2005-06-22 19:29:12.000000', 0),
