(1482702, 187474, 37719, '<td valign="top">Very nice picture and expression for the challenge.  The crop is perfect and the use of sepia nicely sets the tone.  Well done - I gave it a 10.</td>', 'Very nice picture and expression for the challenge.  The crop is perfect and the use of sepia nicely sets the tone.  Well done - I gave it a 10.', '2005-06-25 09:22:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(1482907, 190194, 39243, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by louddog:</b></div><hr/><i> If you need the title to make your photo meet the challenge, you should probably spell check it.  THat being said, there are too many over exposed sections.  It''s a very interesting subject, but the lighting is horrible and I don''t like your choice of composition. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I used spell check an everything seems on the up and up. in fact here is a cut and paste from dictionary.com if this is the word you think needs spell check. <br/> <br/>mau·so·le·um    ( P )  Pronunciation Key  (môs-lm, -z-)<br/>n. pl. mau·so·le·ums or mau·so·le·a (-l) <br/>A large stately tomb or a building housing such a tomb or several tombs. <br/>A gloomy, usually large room or building. <br/> <br/>Other than that I agree with your comments</td>', 'Originally posted by louddog: If you need the title to make your photo meet the challenge, you should probably spell check it.  THat being said, there are too many over exposed sections.  It''s a very interesting subject, but the lighting is horrible and I don''t like your choice of composition.   I used spell check an everything seems on the up and up. in fact here is a cut and paste from dictionary.com if this is the word you think needs spell check.  mau·so·le·um    ( P )  Pronunciation Key  (môs-lm, -z-)n. pl. mau·so·le·ums or mau·so·le·a (-l) A large stately tomb or a building housing such a tomb or several tombs. A gloomy, usually large room or building.  Other than that I agree with your comments', '2005-06-25 12:14:13.000000', NULL, 0),
