(1488704, 190285, 37779, '<td valign="top">Ah, I love the busy, chaos of the weeds and the washed out color. I think to get rid of that sky you could just crop it and it would be pretty neat. It''s almost like a painting, I love it. Thanks for sharing such a great pic.</td>', 'Ah, I love the busy, chaos of the weeds and the washed out color. I think to get rid of that sky you could just crop it and it would be pretty neat. It''s almost like a painting, I love it. Thanks for sharing such a great pic.', '2005-06-28 15:45:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1488793, 189951, 36078, '<td valign="top">From the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I think this is a very powerful image.  Nicely framed and proportioned.  The lack of light at the top left corner and lower corner adds to the effect.  Nice detailed b&amp;w image.<br/> <br/>The window is a little to overpowering for me.  But nice effect on the floor on the light casting.  But I could see how some would like that.  Their is also a slight cant in the window but barely noticeable.  Would have liked to see a bit of dust in the sunlight but it just knit picking.   Very well rounded photo.</td>', 'From the Critique Club I think this is a very powerful image.  Nicely framed and proportioned.  The lack of light at the top left corner and lower corner adds to the effect.  Nice detailed b&w image. The window is a little to overpowering for me.  But nice effect on the floor on the light casting.  But I could see how some would like that.  Their is also a slight cant in the window but barely noticeable.  Would have liked to see a bit of dust in the sunlight but it just knit picking.   Very well rounded photo.', '2005-06-28 16:15:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1489043, 189182, 34659, '<td valign="top">* Greetings from the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>Absolutely met the challenge perfectly!  I really like this image a lot.  Your use of lighting and color was exceptionally well done.  The composition is great - although I think you probably could have cropped a little further to the right (allowing more of the scene to be visible - just a touch).<br/> <br/>I do have to agree with a couple of the other commenters on the red spot in the middle - that is distracting to me, I think mostly because I don''t know what it is.  I think it''d be cool if it was a flame, but I really can''t distinguish what it is.<br/> <br/>Your detail &amp; focus are terrific and the use of reds really brings everything together.  It''s a very dark/demonic/pagan statue that really intrigues the viewer (I think).<br/> <br/>I know that I scored this image highly (8-9 I think), as I remember it vividly from the Darkness Challenge.  I think you did a great job all around.  You have certainly proven your skills with lighting and mood.<br/> <br/>Please don''t hesitate to PM me if you have any questions - I feel privileged to comment on this one!<br/> <br/>Jimmy<br/></td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club * Absolutely met the challenge perfectly!  I really like this image a lot.  Your use of lighting and color was exceptionally well done.  The composition is great - although I think you probably could have cropped a little further to the right (allowing more of the scene to be visible - just a touch). I do have to agree with a couple of the other commenters on the red spot in the middle - that is distracting to me, I think mostly because I don''t know what it is.  I think it''d be cool if it was a flame, but I really can''t distinguish what it is. Your detail & focus are terrific and the use of reds really brings everything together.  It''s a very dark/demonic/pagan statue that really intrigues the viewer (I think). I know that I scored this image highly (8-9 I think), as I remember it vividly from the Darkness Challenge.  I think you did a great job all around.  You have certainly proven your skills with lighting and mood. Please don''t hesitate to PM me if you have any questions - I feel privileged to comment on this one! Jimmy', '2005-06-28 18:11:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(1489084, 189002, 34659, '<td valign="top">* Greetings from the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>First of all, I think this met the Darkness Challenge very well.  Yes, candles were a somewhat common theme for this particular challenge, but I think your shot has some very strong merits - separating it from the rest.<br/> <br/>I like the detail on/in the candle and the flame itself.  The composition is good - except for the fact that the candle''s bottom isn''t horizontal (I''m sure that this probably detracted from your overall score).  Another thing that probably detracted from your score is the background.  As some of the other commenters mentioned, the blue &amp; green dots are distracting and there''s almost enough shadows to the images in the background to make them out, but not quite.  I think a solid black background would have probably done more service to your image.<br/> <br/>I like the soft glow that the flame has (as well as the overall pic''s soft glow) - that adds a very nice warm touch against the dark background.  So, I think you scored some points for "mood" in this piece.  You might consider cropping off the bottom portion of the image until the candle''s bottom can''t be seen - that would eliminate a couple of the issues above.<br/> <br/>Overall, though I think it was a strong entry and with just a couple of modifications could have been a contender.  Nice work.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to PM me with any questions or comments on my feedback.  Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/>Jimmy<br/></td>', '* Greetings from the Critique Club * First of all, I think this met the Darkness Challenge very well.  Yes, candles were a somewhat common theme for this particular challenge, but I think your shot has some very strong merits - separating it from the rest. I like the detail on/in the candle and the flame itself.  The composition is good - except for the fact that the candle''s bottom isn''t horizontal (I''m sure that this probably detracted from your overall score).  Another thing that probably detracted from your score is the background.  As some of the other commenters mentioned, the blue & green dots are distracting and there''s almost enough shadows to the images in the background to make them out, but not quite.  I think a solid black background would have probably done more service to your image. I like the soft glow that the flame has (as well as the overall pic''s soft glow) - that adds a very nice warm touch against the dark background.  So, I think you scored some points for "mood" in this piece.  You might consider cropping off the bottom portion of the image until the candle''s bottom can''t be seen - that would eliminate a couple of the issues above. Overall, though I think it was a strong entry and with just a couple of modifications could have been a contender.  Nice work. Please feel free to PM me with any questions or comments on my feedback.  Just my 2 cents... Jimmy', '2005-06-28 18:30:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1490731, 189002, 37392, '<td valign="top">Thanks for its words, I am in DPChallenge to learn more and more on fotografia, and receiving your certeres comment i learns much. It already makes some of the mentioned modifications and I really feel that it improves much in the image! <br/> <br/>again thanks!<br/> <br/>Martin. <br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by SJCarter:</b></div><hr/><i> * Greetings from the Critique Club *<br/> <br/>First of all, I think this met the Darkness Challenge very well.  Yes, candles were a somewhat common theme for this particular challenge, but I think your shot has some very strong merits - separating it from the rest.<br/> <br/>I like the detail on/in the candle and the flame itself.  The composition is good - except for the fact that the candle''s bottom isn''t horizontal (I''m sure that this probably detracted from your overall score).  Another thing that probably detracted from your score is the background.  As some of the other commenters mentioned, the blue &amp; green dots are distracting and there''s almost enough shadows to the images in the background to make them out, but not quite.  I think a solid black background would have probably done more service to your image.<br/> <br/>I like the soft glow that the flame has (as well as the overall pic''s soft glow) - that adds a very nice warm touch against the dark background.  So, I think you scored some points for "mood" in this piece.  You might consider cropping off the bottom portion of the image until the candle''s bottom can''t be seen - that would eliminate a couple of the issues above.<br/> <br/>Overall, though I think it was a strong entry and with just a couple of modifications could have been a contender.  Nice work.<br/> <br/>Please feel free to PM me with any questions or comments on my feedback.  Just my 2 cents...<br/> <br/>Jimmy </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'Thanks for its words, I am in DPChallenge to learn more and more on fotografia, and receiving your certeres comment i learns much. It already makes some of the mentioned modifications and I really feel that it improves much in the image!  again thanks! Martin.  Originally posted by SJCarter: * Greetings from the Critique Club * First of all, I think this met the Darkness Challenge very well.  Yes, candles were a somewhat common theme for this particular challenge, but I think your shot has some very strong merits - separating it from the rest. I like the detail on/in the candle and the flame itself.  The composition is good - except for the fact that the candle''s bottom isn''t horizontal (I''m sure that this probably detracted from your overall score).  Another thing that probably detracted from your score is the background.  As some of the other commenters mentioned, the blue & green dots are distracting and there''s almost enough shadows to the images in the background to make them out, but not quite.  I think a solid black background would have probably done more service to your image. I like the soft glow that the flame has (as well as the overall pic''s soft glow) - that adds a very nice warm touch against the dark background.  So, I think you scored some points for "mood" in this piece.  You might consider cropping off the bottom portion of the image until the candle''s bottom can''t be seen - that would eliminate a couple of the issues above. Overall, though I think it was a strong entry and with just a couple of modifications could have been a contender.  Nice work. Please feel free to PM me with any questions or comments on my feedback.  Just my 2 cents... Jimmy ', '2005-06-29 10:25:08.000000', NULL, 0),
