(1584284, 189516, 37200, '<td valign="top">disregarding the challenge theme, I think this could use a little more contrast and separation between the headstones and the grass/weeds.  A different B/W conversion method may yield that.  Also, a lower point of view may be a more interesting perspective.  As it is, it''s a decent shot (background sky is a little distracting), and the placement in the challenge is about what I would have guessed.  BTW, thanks for commenting on one of my shots.</td>', 'disregarding the challenge theme, I think this could use a little more contrast and separation between the headstones and the grass/weeds.  A different B/W conversion method may yield that.  Also, a lower point of view may be a more interesting perspective.  As it is, it''s a decent shot (background sky is a little distracting), and the placement in the challenge is about what I would have guessed.  BTW, thanks for commenting on one of my shots.', '2005-08-03 15:33:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(1599928, 190285, 27735, '<td valign="top">Great shot...I gave it a 9!</td>', 'Great shot...I gave it a 9!', '2005-08-10 03:31:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1620929, 188261, 39483, '<td valign="top">Well done! Great composition.<br/>The texture on the leaf really stands out as do the shadows and the other leaf hidding in the corner adds to the photo as well! I wonder how it might look at a slightly different angle to accentuate the center ''curve/bump'' on the leaf itself? Nice B&amp;W!!</td>', 'Well done! Great composition.The texture on the leaf really stands out as do the shadows and the other leaf hidding in the corner adds to the photo as well! I wonder how it might look at a slightly different angle to accentuate the center ''curve/bump'' on the leaf itself? Nice B&W!!', '2005-08-18 10:40:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1623465, 188689, 18932, '<td valign="top">Lovely. Even though the horizon is in the centre of the frame, this is by no means detracts from the photo. It''s slightly distracting for the horizong to go through the head of the photographer - maybe a lower vantage point would have helped. The colour and texture make this shot.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-08-19 08:47:25.</i></td>', 'Lovely. Even though the horizon is in the centre of the frame, this is by no means detracts from the photo. It''s slightly distracting for the horizong to go through the head of the photographer - maybe a lower vantage point would have helped. The colour and texture make this shot.', '2005-08-19 09:46:43.000000', '2005-08-19 09:47:25.000000', 0),
(1631924, 188689, 14986, '<td valign="top">I agree about the angle of the shot, for the purpose of putting the head against full sky.  Other than that, this is truly a beautiful shot that I like very much.  I disagree about the foreground being too busy...I like to see a little detail and some interest there myself.  The mood of the shot is very solitary, even though we know of course that he''s not there alone!</td>', 'I agree about the angle of the shot, for the purpose of putting the head against full sky.  Other than that, this is truly a beautiful shot that I like very much.  I disagree about the foreground being too busy...I like to see a little detail and some interest there myself.  The mood of the shot is very solitary, even though we know of course that he''s not there alone!', '2005-08-22 15:39:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1631930, 188689, 41098, '<td valign="top">Great colors.</td>', 'Great colors.', '2005-08-22 15:40:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(1657072, 188549, 39161, '<td valign="top">Thank you everybody for your reviews!<br/> <br/>Thing is that I never intended to take the best shot on my model, I didn''t even bothered to respect any rule for getting smthing great. It was simply a piece of my mood then.That was all.<br/> <br/>Thank you and good luck!</td>', 'Thank you everybody for your reviews! Thing is that I never intended to take the best shot on my model, I didn''t even bothered to respect any rule for getting smthing great. It was simply a piece of my mood then.That was all. Thank you and good luck!', '2005-08-30 04:07:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(1659145, 189599, 34659, '<td valign="top">It just dawned on me that you shot this...  I just have to reiterate that this IMHO is one of the most underrated shots on the entire site.  There is so much emotion and artistry here that it boggles the mind.  Sure, it''s dark and disturbing, but aren''t some of our strongest thoughts?!?!  I knew there was something missing when I reviewed my Favorites list yesterday - this was it.  Truly a superb, award-winning image.  Kudos...</td>', 'It just dawned on me that you shot this...  I just have to reiterate that this IMHO is one of the most underrated shots on the entire site.  There is so much emotion and artistry here that it boggles the mind.  Sure, it''s dark and disturbing, but aren''t some of our strongest thoughts?!?!  I knew there was something missing when I reviewed my Favorites list yesterday - this was it.  Truly a superb, award-winning image.  Kudos...', '2005-08-30 20:41:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(1678060, 188261, 22459, '<td valign="top">Nice composition love the dark feel to this one almost a Joey Lawrence feel, well done.</td>', 'Nice composition love the dark feel to this one almost a Joey Lawrence feel, well done.', '2005-09-06 03:40:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1679846, 187468, 34659, '<td valign="top">This is such a great shot!  I think it was certainly underrated.  It immediately establishes such a foreboding mood.  Love the tones and composition.  (I scored it an 8 in the challenge.)</td>', 'This is such a great shot!  I think it was certainly underrated.  It immediately establishes such a foreboding mood.  Love the tones and composition.  (I scored it an 8 in the challenge.)', '2005-09-06 19:58:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1711725, 190064, 28710, '<td valign="top">Agreement with other poster. I can''t remember the last time I sat down one evening and cracked a cold one open and just sat there appreciating the raw beauty of molded plastic in the highly functional and stunningly artistic mode we commonly call "chair".<br/> <br/>Truly surpasses good photography to the level of yawn.<br/> <br/>I know that you are particular to good comments, having read your other well thought out and carefully worded critique. <br/> <br/>I''ve used the A75. It can do better than this. Can you?</td>', 'Agreement with other poster. I can''t remember the last time I sat down one evening and cracked a cold one open and just sat there appreciating the raw beauty of molded plastic in the highly functional and stunningly artistic mode we commonly call "chair". Truly surpasses good photography to the level of yawn. I know that you are particular to good comments, having read your other well thought out and carefully worded critique.  I''ve used the A75. It can do better than this. Can you?', '2005-09-15 14:55:10.000000', NULL, 0),
